        {
          "url": "https://docs.oracle.com/en/java/javase/25/docs/api/java.base/java/lang/NullPointerException.html",
          "section": "Class NullPointerException \u2014 operations that throw when an application attempts to use null",
          "retrievedAt": "2026-10-12T21:50:58Z",
          "textSha256": "e733abf770663daa9bff4e1dabe0f2362c50726b3f2179327045c2246f637690"
        },
        {
          "url": "https://maven.apache.org/guides/introduction/introduction-to-the-pom.html",
          "section": "What is a POM? \u2014 the POM is Maven\u2019s fundamental unit of work and specifies dependencies, plugins, and build configuration",
          "retrievedAt": "2026-10-12T21:50:58Z",
          "textSha256": "14333f76b73290167069ef8a699dda5e7d5d91134e907c679055d10e2177b288"
        }
      ],
      "recommendation": "Without adding or removing syllabus rows, make the intake identify a concrete pre-use teaching/scaffolding path: either bind explicit null/NPE and POM/dependency instruction to existing pre-F10 objectives/lab work, or require the F10 project brief to teach and check those concepts before learners apply them. Do not treat merely executing a provided POM as coverage of Maven dependencies.",
      "reviewedSha256": "11334a5eb8dbe7b5eb852951b14c3121d38d78adf6887ca51f453fad6c32f128"
    },
    {
      "id": "java-sme-002",
      "severity": "medium",
      "location": {
        "file": "foundational-track/java-foundations/testing-and-java-review/reading-older-java-code/topic.json",
        "line": 26
      },
      "claim": "Objective o3 overstates backward compatibility by asking learners to predict that code written for Java 8, 11, or 17 still compiles on JDK 25. Source-version age alone cannot establish this: later JDKs remove tools, components, options, and APIs, and application dependencies can also be incompatible.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "url": "https://docs.oracle.com/en/java/javase/25/migrate/removed-tools-and-components.html",
          "section": "Removed Tools and Components \u2014 lists removals in JDK 9 through JDK 25",
          "retrievedAt": "2026-10-12T21:50:58Z",
          "textSha256": "a15df90dfd189f7b8f1ab8abe4a49a3d125837fbe4caa9758cad2f11752a0b56"
        }
      ],
      "recommendation": "Replace the universal prediction with an observable compatibility task, such as identifying the language level and then compiling/testing representative Java 8/11/17 code on JDK 25 while checking removed APIs, options, and dependencies. State that much older source often remains compatible, not that it necessarily compiles.",
      "reviewedSha256": "6345e044ba514dffb203acf5456305a03f53e41fe79124f1cd5b8ed44e40b40b"
    },
    {
      "id": "java-sme-003",
      "severity": "medium",
      "location": {
        "file": "foundational-track/java-foundations/java-basics/strings-and-string-methods/topic.json",
        "line": 26
      },
      "claim": "Objective o3 says \u201ca String method returns a new string,\u201d but the methods named in o2 include length, charAt, and indexOf, which return int or char, while String-returning methods promise a String value rather than a newly allocated object. The accurate invariant is that a String value cannot be changed after creation.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "url": "https://docs.oracle.com/en/java/javase/25/docs/api/java.base/java/lang/String.html",
          "section": "Class String and method summaries \u2014 Strings are constant; length/charAt/indexOf return non-String values and transformations return String values",
          "retrievedAt": "2026-10-12T21:50:43Z",
          "textSha256": "d6fe54ea59fc2c32b57df32f03ec3af06d0c95043fb1c284d7d30a890b5729e2"
        }
      ],
      "recommendation": "Rewrite o3 to explain that String objects are immutable: inspecting methods may return numbers or characters, and transformation methods return a String value without changing the receiver; do not promise a newly allocated String object.",
      "reviewedSha256": "e0f1c973f039da27ee98005e10a13ed1751bec5df9610a44c427050af99b3774"
    },
    {
